\title{Collection expressions}

\date{2026-06-12T16:34:15Z}
\import{swarm-macros}
\p{A \em{collection expression} is one of:

\ul{
  \li{the empty collection #{\varnothing},}
  \li{a collection variable #{\delta} (in general, different metavariables are used for different types of collections),}
  \li{a singleton collection, denoted #{\{e\}}, or}
  \li{the union of two collection expressions, #{\Delta_1 \cup \Delta_2},}
}

quotiented by the assumption that #{(\cup, \varnothing)} are a monoid;
\em{i.e.} #{\cup} is associative, and #{\varnothing} is an identity
for #{\cup}.  Put another way, collection expressions are a free
commutative monoid over XXX

XXX \em{free extension}!

XXX what to do about provisioning oracle etc.?  Come up with some examples of how it ought to work?

}

